From: EasyStick maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] sdio: transmit exact packet length without 512-byte block padding

The ESP-Hosted-NG host driver previously padded every outgoing frame to a
multiple of 512 bytes (ESP_BLOCK_SIZE), reading beyond the allocated skb
boundary into uninitialized memory and forcing all transfers into SDIO block
mode.

On ESP32-C6 SDIO slave, repeated CMD53 block-mode writes cause the SLC DMA
descriptor chain to lose internal synchronization, permanently asserting
DAT0 busy and resulting in communications failure (Espressif EHM-188).

Transmit exact 4-byte-aligned frame length without 512-byte block padding.
Frames <= 512 bytes are transferred via SDIO byte mode, avoiding the C6
SLC block-mode DMA descriptor synchronization bug.

---
 sdio/esp_sdio.c | 10 ++++------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

--- a/sdio/esp_sdio.c
+++ b/sdio/esp_sdio.c
@@ -1150,24 +1150,23 @@
 		data_left = len_to_send = 0;
 
 		data_left = tx_skb->len;
-		pad = ESP_BLOCK_SIZE - (data_left % ESP_BLOCK_SIZE);
-		data_left += pad;
+		(void)pad;
+		(void)block_cnt;
 
 
 		do {
-			block_cnt = data_left / ESP_BLOCK_SIZE;
-			len_to_send = data_left;
+			len_to_send = (data_left + 3) & (~3);
 			esp_info("CMD53_TX: addr=0x%x bytes=%u\n",
 				 ESP_SLAVE_CMD53_END_ADDR - len_to_send, len_to_send);
 			ret = esp_write_block(context, ESP_SLAVE_CMD53_END_ADDR - len_to_send,
-					pos, (len_to_send + 3) & (~3), ACQUIRE_LOCK);
+					pos, len_to_send, ACQUIRE_LOCK);
 
 			if (ret) {
 				esp_err("Failed to send data: %d %d %d\n", ret, len_to_send, data_left);
 				break;
 			}
 
-			data_left -= len_to_send;
+			data_left = 0;
 			pos += len_to_send;
 		} while (data_left);
 
